   "name": "Coefficients and subscripts",
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "A formula has a qualitative meaning, which elements, and a quantitative meaning, how many. The coefficient in front counts atoms or molecules: 3H₂O is three water molecules. The subscript after a symbol counts atoms in one molecule: Cl₂ has two chlorine atoms."
    }
   },
